 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the town of Clarkstown in Rockland county to\nalienate certain lands used as parklands for the purposes of installing a\ncellular tower",
    "basePrintNo": "S10522",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10522-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Rockland County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10522\n\nSPONSOR: WEBER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the town of Clarkstown in Rockland\ncounty to alienate certain lands used as parklands for the purposes of\ninstalling a cellular tower\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would authorize the Town of Clarkstown to alienate certain\nlands for the purpose of installing a cellular tower.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one would authorize the Town of Clarkstown to alienate certain\nlands for the purpose of installing a cellular tower and that all\nproceeds from the lease shall be used for capital improvements to exist-\ning park and recreational facilities or for the acquisition of addi-\ntional park or recreational facilities.\n\nSection two outlines the boundaries of the parcel of land authorized by\nsection one to be leased.\n\nSection three states that if the land described in section two ceases to\nbe used for the purposes detailed in section one, the lease shall be\nterminated, and the land shall revert back to the Town of Clarkstown for\npark and recreational purposes.\n\nSection four states that if the Town of Clarkstown receives any federal\nassistance or funds for the purchase, maintenance or improvement of the\nparklands set forth in section two, the discontinuance and alienation of\nsuch parkland authorized by the provisions of this act shall not occur\nuntil the Town of Clarkstown has complied with any and all federal\nrequirements pertaining to the alienation or conversion of parkland,\nincluding satisfying all the conditions set forth by the secretary of\nthe interior.\n\nSection five sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill was introduced at the request of the Town of Clarkstown as the\ninstallation of a new cellular tower would be beneficial for residents.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
